---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import {catalogue} from "../lib/catalogue";
---
<Layout title="A clearer path through your degree">
<section class="hero">
<div class="hero-copy"><p class="eyebrow"><span class="gold-dot"></span> YOUR NEXT SEMESTER STARTS HERE</p><h1>Your degree.<br/><em>A clearer path.</em></h1><p class="hero-description">Find the courses you want to study.<br/>Understand which ones actually count.</p><p class="muted hero-note">Your commencement year. Your completed study.<br/>One plan that brings it all together.</p><div class="hero-actions"><form method="post" action="/api/action"><input type="hidden" name="action" value="demo"/><button class="button primary">Explore an example plan <span>↗</span></button></form><a class="text-link" href="/explore">Browse the catalogue →</a></div><p class="fine">No account needed to try · Fictional student records</p></div>
<div class="hero-preview" aria-label="Example of a student degree plan"><div class="preview-top"><span class="eyebrow">A PLAN THAT KNOWS YOUR CONTEXT</span><span class="small-pill">2025 rules</span></div><h2>Master of Computing</h2><p>Human-Centred & Creative Computing</p><div class="preview-progress"><span><strong>36</strong> / 96 units completed</span><span>Every course, accounted for.</span></div><div class="progress-track"><span style="width:37.5%"></span></div><div class="preview-semester"><span>YOUR NEXT SEMESTER</span><span>12 units planned</span></div><div class="preview-course"><span class="course-icon">◎</span><div><small>COMP8610 · 6 UNITS</small><strong>Computer Graphics</strong><span class="positive">✓ Fits your specialisation</span></div><span class="preview-arrow">↗</span></div><div class="preview-course"><span class="course-icon">⌘</span><div><small>COMP8020 · 6 UNITS</small><strong>Advanced Topics in HCC</strong><span class="amber">◷ Check permission to enrol</span></div><span class="preview-arrow">↗</span></div><div class="preview-foot"><span>✧</span> See what counts. Understand why.</div></div>
</section>
<section class="principles" aria-label="How the planner helps"><article><span class="step">01</span><h2>The right rules, always.</h2><p>Your degree follows your commencement year, even when the course catalogue moves on.</p></article><article><span class="step">02</span><h2>More than a unit counter.</h2><p>Bring completed study, credit and exemptions together. See the requirements you still need to meet.</p></article><article><span class="step">03</span><h2>A reason for every choice.</h2><p>Separate what counts, what you can enrol in, and what is offered next semester.</p></article></section>
<section class="catalogue-callout"><div><p class="eyebrow">EXPLORE YOUR POSSIBILITIES</p><h2>The university, within reach.</h2><p>Browse {catalogue.length.toLocaleString()} course, program and subplan entries across 2025–2027.</p></div><a class="button secondary" href="/explore">Find your next course ↗</a></section>
</Layout>